---
import SketchSheet from '../design/SketchSheet.astro';
import '../design/design-aids.css';
const cases = [
  { label:'A · Before a durable commit', log:'Update record survives; no commit record survives.', table:'May already contain the 22.00 version as well as 20.00.', reply:'No success received.', result:'20.00', reason:'Without a surviving commit record, PostgreSQL treats the transaction as uncommitted. Queries cannot see its 22.00 version.' },
  { label:'B · After the log flush', log:'Update and commit records survive.', table:'Still has the earlier page with 20.00 only.', reply:'Success received.', result:'22.00', reason:'Recovery restores the 22.00 version from WAL. Queries can see it because the commit record survived too.' },
  { label:'C · Before the reply arrives', log:'Update and commit records survive.', table:'Still has the earlier page with 20.00 only.', reply:'Connection lost before any success arrived.', result:'22.00', reason:'The transaction committed, but the application never received confirmation.' },
];
---
<figure class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface" aria-labelledby="crash-outcomes-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · Recovery outcomes</span>
  <h3 id="crash-outcomes-title">Three crash scenarios</h3>
  <p>In each case, a transaction changes P7’s price from 20.00 to 22.00. The server crashes, loses memory and restarts with its storage intact. No other transaction changes P7.</p>
  <div class="histories">{cases.map(item => <SketchSheet><h4>{item.label}</h4><dl><div><dt>Durable WAL</dt><dd>{item.log}</dd></div><div><dt>Table file at the crash</dt><dd>{item.table}</dd></div><div><dt>Application’s reply</dt><dd>{item.reply}</dd></div></dl><p class="outcome">New query after recovery: <strong>{item.result}</strong></p><p class="reason">{item.reason}</p></SketchSheet>)}</div>
  <figcaption>These examples use synchronous local commit and reliable storage. In B and C, a query after recovery returns 22.00. In C, the application lost its connection before it could learn that the transaction committed.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .histories { display:grid; gap:1.2rem; margin-top:1.3rem; }
  dl { margin:0; }
  dl > div { display:grid; grid-template-columns:9.5rem minmax(0,1fr); gap:1rem; padding:.55rem 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule); }
  dt { color:var(--color-text-secondary); font-size:.8rem; }
  dd { margin:0; font-size:.85rem; }
  .outcome { padding:.6rem .8rem; background:var(--paper-match); border-left:2px solid var(--teal); font-size:.85rem; }
  .outcome strong { font-family:var(--font-mono); }
  .reason { font-size:.85rem; }
  @media(max-width:550px) { dl > div { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:.15rem; } }
</style>
